IMPORT policy

-- Per the standing preamble: every field not directly probed by a question is set
-- so that (a) no exclusion unrelated to the question fires, and (b) every condition
-- for coverage unrelated to the question is met. The default "unrelated" values used
-- throughout are: age 40 (well under the 80 exclusion), and hospitalization/wellness
-- visit/confirmation all at month 1 (well inside every deadline in Section 1.3, and
-- well inside the 12-month policy term).

-- Q1: hospitalized by burns suffered while doing my duty as a firefighter.
-- Causal link to firefighter service is explicit ("while doing my duty as a
-- firefighter") -> the fire-fighter exclusion (2.1.3) applies.
q1 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at the time of hospitalization`                                                  IS 40
    `months after the effective date when the hospitalization occurred`                   IS 1
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit occurred`                    IS 1
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit was confirmed to the insurer` IS 1
    `due to skydiving`                                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the military`                                                       IS FALSE
    `due to service as a fire fighter`                                                     IS TRUE
    `due to service in the police`                                                         IS FALSE
    `for sickness`                                                                         IS FALSE
    `for accidental injury`                                                                IS TRUE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding of information`                    IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q1

-- Q2: 78 years old at the time of hospitalization. Cause not specified by the
-- question, so treated as an otherwise-ordinary covered sickness. 78 is below the
-- age-80 exclusion threshold.
q2 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at the time of hospitalization`                                                  IS 78
    `months after the effective date when the hospitalization occurred`                   IS 1
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit occurred`                    IS 1
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit was confirmed to the insurer` IS 1
    `due to skydiving`                                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the military`                                                       IS FALSE
    `due to service as a fire fighter`                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the police`                                                         IS FALSE
    `for sickness`                                                                         IS TRUE
    `for accidental injury`                                                                IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding of information`                    IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q2

-- Q3: pneumonia (sickness), 5 months after the effective date, age 65. At 5 months
-- the Section 1.3 confirmation deadline (month 7) has not yet arrived, so condition
-- 1.3 is "still pending" regardless of the (unspecified) wellness-visit facts.
q3 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at the time of hospitalization`                                                  IS 65
    `months after the effective date when the hospitalization occurred`                   IS 5
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit occurred`                    IS 1
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit was confirmed to the insurer` IS 1
    `due to skydiving`                                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the military`                                                       IS FALSE
    `due to service as a fire fighter`                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the police`                                                         IS FALSE
    `for sickness`                                                                         IS TRUE
    `for accidental injury`                                                                IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding of information`                    IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q3

-- Q4: a fall while traveling abroad (accidental injury; §3.1 covers the whole world,
-- so "abroad" is not itself a problem); confirmation of the wellness visit was given
-- 8 months after the effective date. Past tense ("I had given") places the
-- hospitalization at or after that same point, i.e. after the 7-month deadline —
-- and 8 is later than both the 6-month (visit) and 7-month (confirmation) limbs of
-- condition 1.3, so it fails outright regardless of which limb is decisive.
q4 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at the time of hospitalization`                                                  IS 40
    `months after the effective date when the hospitalization occurred`                   IS 8
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit occurred`                    IS 8
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit was confirmed to the insurer` IS 8
    `due to skydiving`                                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the military`                                                       IS FALSE
    `due to service as a fire fighter`                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the police`                                                         IS FALSE
    `for sickness`                                                                         IS FALSE
    `for accidental injury`                                                                IS TRUE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding of information`                    IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q4

-- Q5: hospitalized for punching my own face to show off for friends; no fraud or
-- misrepresentation. The fraud flag is set FALSE exactly as stated -- the question
-- is not really about fraud. Modelled instead as neither "sickness" nor "accidental
-- injury": punching one's own face is a deliberate act, not an accident, so it does
-- not fall within the 1.1 insuring clause at all. See NOTES.md -- this is the most
-- contestable judgement call in this encoding.
q5 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at the time of hospitalization`                                                  IS 40
    `months after the effective date when the hospitalization occurred`                   IS 1
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit occurred`                    IS 1
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit was confirmed to the insurer` IS 1
    `due to skydiving`                                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the military`                                                       IS FALSE
    `due to service as a fire fighter`                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the police`                                                         IS FALSE
    `for sickness`                                                                         IS FALSE
    `for accidental injury`                                                                IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding of information`                    IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q5

-- Q6: skydiving injury (2.1.1 exclusion, dispositive on its own); age 79 (under the
-- age-80 exclusion, so age alone would not exclude); wellness-visit proof given 6.5
-- months after the effective date (also independently late against the 6-month
-- visit limb of condition 1.3). Covered should be FALSE via skydiving regardless of
-- how the age/visit facts are read.
q6 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at the time of hospitalization`                                                  IS 79
    `months after the effective date when the hospitalization occurred`                   IS 6.5
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit occurred`                    IS 6.5
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit was confirmed to the insurer` IS 6.5
    `due to skydiving`                                                                     IS TRUE
    `due to service in the military`                                                       IS FALSE
    `due to service as a fire fighter`                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the police`                                                         IS FALSE
    `for sickness`                                                                         IS FALSE
    `for accidental injury`                                                                IS TRUE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding of information`                    IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q6

-- Q7: heart attack (sickness), wellness-visit proof submitted 2 months after the
-- effective date (comfortably inside both Section 1.3 limbs), age 75 (under 80).
-- No exclusion applies.
q7 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at the time of hospitalization`                                                  IS 75
    `months after the effective date when the hospitalization occurred`                   IS 2
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit occurred`                    IS 2
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit was confirmed to the insurer` IS 2
    `due to skydiving`                                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the military`                                                       IS FALSE
    `due to service as a fire fighter`                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the police`                                                         IS FALSE
    `for sickness`                                                                         IS TRUE
    `for accidental injury`                                                                IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding of information`                    IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q7

-- Q8: injured in a military training exercise (2.1.2 exclusion: a training exercise
-- is service in the military); hospitalization occurred within the policy term (set
-- to month 6, i.e. inside the 12-month term); no fraud.
q8 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at the time of hospitalization`                                                  IS 40
    `months after the effective date when the hospitalization occurred`                   IS 6
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit occurred`                    IS 1
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit was confirmed to the insurer` IS 1
    `due to skydiving`                                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the military`                                                       IS TRUE
    `due to service as a fire fighter`                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the police`                                                         IS FALSE
    `for sickness`                                                                         IS FALSE
    `for accidental injury`                                                                IS TRUE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding of information`                    IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q8

-- Q9: hospitalized because the claimant's son bit their ankle; wellness-visit proof
-- given 6 months after the effective date (exactly on the boundary of both Section
-- 1.3 limbs -- "no later than" is read inclusively, so this is timely); serving as a
-- police officer at the time of hospitalization. The police exclusion (2.1.4) is
-- read as requiring the injury to arise from police service, not merely that the
-- claimant held that job at the time -- a domestic dog/child-type bite has no causal
-- connection to police duties, so the exclusion does not apply. See NOTES.md.
q9 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at the time of hospitalization`                                                  IS 40
    `months after the effective date when the hospitalization occurred`                   IS 6
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit occurred`                    IS 6
    `months after the effective date when the wellness visit was confirmed to the insurer` IS 6
    `due to skydiving`                                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the military`                                                       IS FALSE
    `due to service as a fire fighter`                                                     IS FALSE
    `due to service in the police`                                                         IS FALSE
    `for sickness`                                                                         IS FALSE
    `for accidental injury`                                                                IS TRUE
    `fraud or misrepresentation or material withholding of information`                    IS FALSE
#EVAL `covered` q9
